---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import ModelFigure from '../components/figures/ModelFigure.astro';
import Timeline from '../components/figures/Timeline.astro';
import ArticleEnd from '../components/journal/ArticleEnd.astro';
import ArticleHead from '../components/journal/ArticleHead.astro';
import Caption from '../components/journal/Caption.astro';
import Cite from '../components/journal/Cite.astro';
import JSection from '../components/journal/JSection.astro';
import NextSteps from '../components/journal/NextSteps.astro';
import Figure from '../components/site/Figure.astro';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
import { leaders } from '../data/people';
import { awards } from '../data/research';
import { accArticle } from '../data/site';
import { photo } from '../lib/photos';

const numbers = [
	{ measure: 'Workshops held', y2024: '16', y2025: '20' },
	{ measure: 'Peer-reviewed papers by mentees', y2024: '150+', y2025: '150+' },
	{ measure: 'Conference abstracts accepted', y2024: '100+', y2025: '100+' },
	{ measure: 'Match Mentorship cohort that matched', y2024: '90%', y2025: '80%' },
];

const sections = [
	{ id: 'introduction', label: 'Introduction' },
	{ id: 'model', label: 'The model' },
	{ id: 'history', label: 'Ten years' },
	{ id: 'recognition', label: 'Recognition' },
	{ id: 'leadership', label: 'Leadership' },
	{ id: 'mission', label: 'Mission' },
];

const refs = [
	{ text: 'Khan MS. Fostering the next generation of physician-scientists in developing countries. American College of Cardiology, Fellows in Training Section. January 22, 2024.', href: accArticle },
	{ text: 'Research Consultancy. The year in review, 2024 and 2025.', href: 'https://www.facebook.com/researchconsultancyrc' },
	{ text: 'Research Consultancy. Match Mentorship results, 2025 and 2026.', href: 'https://www.facebook.com/researchconsultancyrc' },
];
---

<Layout title="About us" description="Why physician-scientists set up Research Consultancy in 2016, how its mentoring model works, and what ten years of it have produced.">
	<ArticleHead
		type="Perspective"
		title="Why we teach research to medical students"
		dek="Physician-scientists set up Research Consultancy in 2016 to teach research methods to students who were not being taught them. This is how the model works and what ten years of it have produced."
		sections={sections}
	>
		<div slot="byline" class="mt-7 max-w-[40rem]">
			<p class="j-byline">M. Shahzeb Khan, MD, MS<sup>1</sup>; Kaneez Fatima, MD<sup>1</sup>; M. Shariq Usman, MD<sup>2</sup>; Tariq Jamal Siddiqi, MD<sup>1</sup></p>
			<p class="j-affil mt-1"><sup>1</sup>Baylor Scott &amp; White, Dallas, Texas. <sup>2</sup>UT Southwestern Medical Center, Dallas, Texas.</p>
		</div>
		<Figure slot="aside" src="events/leadership-group.jpg" alt="RC faculty standing together at a scientific meeting" label="Figure 1" caption="RC faculty at a scientific meeting." imgClass="aspect-[4/3]" loading="eager" sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 20rem, 100vw" />
	</ArticleHead>

	<JSection title="Introduction" id="introduction">
		<div class="j-main j-prose">
			<p class="drop-cap">
				Each year, many international medical graduates apply for U.S. residency with strong scores and little research.
				The cause is usually training, not ability. Most medical schools outside the United States treat research as an
				extra, and students who want to learn it rarely find a mentor.<Cite n={1} />
			</p>
			<p>
				RC's founders trained at U.S. institutions and built research careers there. In 2016 they began teaching what
				they had learned, in practical workshops for beginners followed by long-term mentorship. When the pandemic moved
				classes onto Zoom in 2020, students from any country could join.<Cite n={1} />
			</p>
		</div>
		<aside class="j-margin">
			<div class="border border-navy bg-[#f5f8fb]">
				<p class="bg-navy px-3 py-1.5 text-[12.5px] font-semibold text-white">Research in context</p>
				<dl class="space-y-3 p-3 text-[13px] leading-relaxed">
					<div><dt class="font-semibold text-navy">Evidence before RC</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 font-serif text-[14px] text-ink-secondary">Research training for medical students outside the United States was scarce and rarely mentored.</dd></div>
					<div><dt class="font-semibold text-navy">Added value</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 font-serif text-[14px] text-ink-secondary">Courses end in real projects, supervised by physician-scientists who publish in the same field.</dd></div>
					<div><dt class="font-semibold text-navy">Implications</dt><dd class="mt-0.5 font-serif text-[14px] text-ink-secondary">A student with no research experience can publish within a year. One mentee published 35 papers in just over a year after Level 1.</dd></div>
				</dl>
			</div>
		</aside>
	</JSection>

	<JSection title="The model" id="model">
		<div class="j-main j-prose">
			<p>
				RC runs on near-peer mentorship (Figure 2). Faculty mentor near-peers, and near-peers mentor students. Because
				mentors come from the student tier, the model grows: many of today's mentors were RC students, and more than 20
				have moved on to U.S. postdoctoral posts.<Cite n={1} />
			</p>
		</div>
		<ModelFigure class="j-main mt-4" label="Figure 2" />
	</JSection>

	<JSection title="Ten years" id="history">
		<div class="j-main j-prose">
			<p>
				Figure 3 shows the main milestones. By 2024, RC had mentored more than 3,500 students, 70% of them women and a
				third from rural areas, and mentees had published more than 600 papers.<Cite n={1} /> Table 1 shows the two most
				recent years.<Cite n={2} />
			</p>
		</div>
		<Timeline class="j-span mt-6" label="Figure 3" />
		<figure class="j-main mt-10">
			<Caption label="Table 1" title="RC in numbers, 2024 and 2025." class="j-caption-top" />
			<table class="j-table">
				<thead><tr><th scope="col">Measure</th><th scope="col" class="text-right">2024</th><th scope="col" class="text-right">2025</th></tr></thead>
				<tbody>
					{numbers.map((n) => (
						<tr><th scope="row" class="font-normal">{n.measure}</th><td class="text-right tabular-nums">{n.y2024}</td><td class="text-right tabular-nums">{n.y2025}</td></tr>
					))}
				</tbody>
			</table>
			<p class="j-tablenote">Match figures are for the 2024-25 and 2025-26 cohorts.<Cite n={3} /></p>
		</figure>
	</JSection>

	<JSection title="Recognition" id="recognition">
		<dl class="j-main divide-y divide-hairline border-y border-hairline">
			{awards.map((a) => (
				<div class="grid gap-1 py-3.5 sm:grid-cols-[13rem_1fr] sm:gap-6">
					<dt class="font-semibold">{a.title}</dt>
					<dd class="font-serif text-[15.5px] leading-relaxed text-ink-secondary">{a.detail}</dd>
				</div>
			))}
		</dl>
	</JSection>

	<JSection title="Leadership" id="leadership">
		<ul class="j-span grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-5 gap-y-8 lg:grid-cols-4">
			{leaders.map((p) => (
				<li>
					<Image src={photo(p.photo)} alt={`Portrait of ${p.name}`} widths={[300, 600]} sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 20vw, 45vw" class="aspect-[4/5] w-full object-cover object-top" />
					<p class="mt-3 text-[13px] font-semibold text-label">{p.role}</p>
					<p class="font-semibold">{p.name}</p>
					<p class="mt-0.5 text-[13.5px] leading-snug text-ink-muted">{p.title}, {p.place}</p>
				</li>
			))}
		</ul>
		<p class="j-span text-[14.5px]"><a href={withBase('/mentors')} class="link">Read the faculty biographies</a></p>
	</JSection>

	<JSection title="Mission" id="mission">
		<dl class="j-main grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
			<div class="border-t-[3px] border-navy pt-3">
				<dt class="j-subhead">Vision</dt>
				<dd class="mt-2 font-serif text-[1.1875rem] leading-snug">Physician-scientists from every country, with fair access to research training.</dd>
			</div>
			<div class="border-t-[3px] border-orange pt-3">
				<dt class="j-subhead">Mission</dt>
				<dd class="mt-2 font-serif text-[1.1875rem] leading-snug">To train and mentor medical students and doctors from their first study to their first match.</dd>
			</div>
		</dl>
	</JSection>

	<NextSteps />

	<ArticleEnd refs={refs} citeTitle="Why we teach research to medical students" contributions="All four authors founded or lead Research Consultancy and teach its courses. Near-peer mentors and research analysts run the project groups." />
</Layout>
